    {
      "id": "claim_b10dfe2a80804cda803493e4f58e2c06",
      "statement": "Per-issue workspaces are `<git.Root>/.sebastian/workspaces/<issueNumber>` on branch `sebastian/issue-<n>`; if the directory already exists it is returned unchanged (the previous run's uncommitted agent work must not be deleted), and only when it is missing does preparation run `worktree prune` then `worktree add -B <branch> <path> main` from local main, where `-B` re-points a leftover branch ref instead of failing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L88-L104",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:51fb2ed010c301c869f200f67b9353fe0a918306bc336b09de4a14e620da3533:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Libs/Git.cs#L85-L93",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:acf45de8dd40b9ac3c494f32b181a35b6fa6cef1ec1dac9cd2e683777c390348:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c776f6539a374e56ac0a88781addcee8",
      "statement": "Preparation deliberately does not serialize against the push-webhook sync, which takes no semaphore: a documented shortcut accepts that a concurrent `merge --ff-only` and `worktree add` can collide on `.git/index.lock`, in which case the losing job fails with an InvalidOperationException while the repository stays consistent.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Libs/Git.cs#L118-L118",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:600f5ffac9e2fd0d35a7dc4b38ac73b3165d2d2c23bd06352d3e35a0cf17b9fd:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Libs/Git.cs#L180-L208",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3a1d1876e6b08c2e059a92aa3f8b8026bf6ff3fc38f08838f28fce945d2a34fe:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f7e33d252a514815a663c0dd16b16b67",
      "statement": "The git layer never commits, pushes, creates pull requests, or resolves conflicts — its entire verb set is fetch, merge --ff-only, worktree add/prune, status, rev-parse, rev-list, remote get-url, and branch --show-current — and the prohibition is stated independently in ImplementationAgent's fixed Instructions and in ImplementSpec.BuildPrompt, with a shell deny-list covering only the destructive subset.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L112-L132",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9b6800bf753ee018f2eebd3dcee9ccd4efcf2bf77182bbcb3f22dc77baa8ffb9:"
        },
        {
