    {
      "id": "claim_438763de2c784d65b6a871e1803d0d54",
      "statement": "Pinning the content root to the repository toplevel and parsing origin into RepositoryIdentity happen in EnsureRepositoryAsync, which throws on failure; RepositoryIdentity is assigned only after the parse succeeds and is never cleared, so a null Git.Repository means the hosted service has not finished starting (ImplementSpec then throws \"Git repository is not initialized. The Git hosted service has not started.\").",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L68-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ea4e13bacb2d891e2765a7076250f8ac81a0138ee43235b7279fd0ec17749cf6:"
